# Impeccable Design System

This project follows an Impeccable-inspired UI workflow for a modern Vietnamese travel website.

The goal is not to make the UI flashy.  
The goal is to make it clear, refined, fast, resilient, and easy to use.

## Project Context

This is a travel website for learning and portfolio purposes.

The UI should feel:

- clean
- premium
- image-driven
- calm
- trustworthy
- easy to scan
- beginner-friendly in code

Use Vietnamese comments for important logic.

## Core Constraints

- Do not change routes unless asked
- Do not remove search, filter, or sort
- Do not change business logic unless asked
- Do not invent unnecessary features
- Prefer Tailwind CSS
- Keep code readable for a first-year Computer Science student
- Preserve existing data structure unless change is required
- Always handle responsive behavior

## Recommended Workflow

When redesigning or improving UI, follow this order:

1. Shape
2. Clarify
3. Distill
4. Layout
5. Typeset
6. Colorize
7. Bolder / Quieter
8. Craft
9. Animate
10. Delight
11. Adapt
12. Harden
13. Optimize
14. Polish
15. Audit
16. Critique
17. Document
18. Extract
19. Live
20. Teach

## 1. Shape

Before coding, understand the UI task.

Ask:

- What is this screen or component for?
- Who is using it?
- What action should the user take?
- What content is shown?
- What can be missing, long, short, or dynamic?
- What feeling should the UI create?

For this travel website, prefer:

- inspiring
- clear
- calm
- premium
- friendly

## 2. Clarify

The user should never have to guess.

- Use clear labels
- Make actions obvious
- Avoid vague wording like "More", "Options", "Click here"
- Use clear empty, loading, and error states
- Group related content logically

Good examples:

- "Xem chi tiết địa điểm"
- "Lọc theo ngân sách"
- "Không tìm thấy địa điểm phù hợp"

## 3. Distill

Less, but better.

- Remove unnecessary labels
- Remove duplicated information
- Shorten long text
- Keep only what helps the user decide
- Each section should have one main purpose

Avoid clutter.

## 4. Layout

The layout should breathe.

Use:

- `max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8`
- `py-16`, `py-20`, `gap-6`, `gap-8`
- `grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`

Rules:

- Group related elements closer together
- Separate unrelated sections with more space
- Avoid random spacing
- The user should know where to look first within 2 seconds

## 5. Typeset

Text must be readable and scannable.

Use:

- Page title: `text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900`
- Section title: `text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900`
- Card title: `text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900`
- Body: `text-slate-600 leading-relaxed`
- Meta: `text-slate-500`

Rules:

- Avoid long paragraphs
- Use `max-w-2xl` or `max-w-3xl` for long text
- Prefer `text-left` for body content
- Use short paragraphs and bullet points when helpful

## 6. Colorize

Color organizes information. It is not decoration.

Use neutral colors first:

- Background: `bg-slate-50` or `bg-sky-50`
- Card: `bg-white`
- Main text: `text-slate-900`
- Body text: `text-slate-600`
- Muted text: `text-slate-500`

Use one primary color:

- `sky`
- `cyan`
- `teal`

Use one accent color for CTA:

- `amber`
- `orange`

Rules:

- Do not create rainbow UI
- Same color should mean same thing
- CTA color should be used sparingly
- Text must have strong contrast

## 7. Bolder and Quieter

Use both intentionally.

Bolder means making important things clearer:

- bigger title
- stronger contrast
- clearer CTA
- more spacing around important actions

Quieter means reducing noise:

- mute secondary text
- reduce unnecessary borders
- reduce excessive shadows
- remove unnecessary icons

Rule:

Only the important thing should stand out.  
Everything else should support it quietly.

## 8. Craft

Craft is precision and refinement.

Check:

- spacing
- alignment
- icon sizes
- text hierarchy
- card consistency
- image cropping
- hover states

Avoid random values.

Use consistent patterns:

- Cards: `rounded-2xl` or `rounded-3xl`
- Shadows: `shadow-sm`, `shadow-md`, `hover:shadow-lg`
- Transitions: `transition-all duration-300 ease-out`

## 9. Animate

Animation must support clarity, not decoration.

Good motion:

- `transition-all duration-300 ease-out`
- `hover:-translate-y-1`
- `hover:shadow-lg`
- fade + small translate for entry

Avoid:

- bounce
- spin
- aggressive zoom
- animating everything

Use transform and opacity when possible.

## 10. Delight

Delight should be subtle, useful, and non-disruptive.

Good delight:

- smooth hover feedback
- helpful empty states
- skeleton loading
- clear input focus

Bad delight:

- surprise popups
- loud animation
- unnecessary delay
- distracting effects

## 11. Adapt

UI must adapt to screen size, content, and state.

Handle:

- mobile
- tablet
- desktop
- long text
- missing image
- empty result
- loading state
- error state

Use:

- `line-clamp-2`
- `truncate`
- responsive grids
- image fallback
- empty states

## 12. Harden

Assume things will fail.

Always handle:

- loading
- success
- empty
- error

Rules:

- No broken image icons
- No blank page
- No overflowing text
- No layout breaking on mobile
- No crash from missing data

Reliability beats fancy UI.

## 13. Optimize

Performance is part of UX.

Rules:

- Use `next/image` when possible
- Use correct image sizes
- Lazy load when appropriate
- Avoid heavy animations
- Avoid unnecessary libraries
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Prefer transform and opacity for animation

The UI should feel fast and responsive.

## 14. Polish

Polish means fixing small rough edges.

Check:

- spacing feels balanced
- hover feels smooth
- buttons align well
- cards look consistent
- text hierarchy is clear
- images crop well
- mobile layout feels natural

If something feels slightly off, refine it.

## 15. Audit

Review the UI like a first-time user.

Check:

- Is the page clear within 2 seconds?
- Is the primary action obvious?
- Is the layout overwhelming?
- Is text readable?
- Is search/filter easy to use?
- Does mobile work well?
- Are empty states helpful?
- Are images reliable?

Find friction and fix it.

## 16. Critique

Give specific, actionable feedback.

Use this format:

- Issue:
- Why it matters:
- Suggestion:

Avoid vague feedback like:

- "looks good"
- "make it nicer"
- "modernize it"

Focus on clarity, hierarchy, spacing, visual weight, interaction, and consistency.

## 17. Document

When creating a reusable UI pattern, document the decision.

Examples:

- Card pattern
- Button style
- Layout container
- Color usage
- Empty state style

Keep documentation practical and short.

## 18. Extract

If a UI pattern repeats, extract it.

Examples:

- `Container`
- `SectionHeader`
- `Button`
- `DestinationCard`
- `EmptyState`

Avoid copy-pasting repeated UI.

Do not over-engineer.  
Extract only when reuse is clear.

## 19. Live

Design must work in real usage.

Before considering UI done:

- test locally
- test mobile view
- test real browser
- test slow network if possible
- deploy early
- gather feedback

Real usage reveals the truth.

## 20. Teach

Make the code and system understandable.

Rules:

- Use clear component names
- Add Vietnamese comments for important logic
- Avoid clever code
- Prefer readable structure
- Use examples when documenting patterns

If the system cannot be explained, it cannot be maintained.

## Travel Website UI Direction

For this project:

- Light theme
- Spacious layout
- Strong travel imagery
- Clean cards
- Clear search and filters
- Friendly Vietnamese content
- Premium but not overly complex

Recommended card style:

- `bg-white`
- `rounded-2xl`
- `shadow-sm hover:shadow-lg`
- `transition-all duration-300 ease-out`
- `hover:-translate-y-1`
- image with `aspect-video object-cover`
- title in `text-slate-900`
- meta in `text-slate-500`
- description in `text-slate-600`

Recommended button style:

- Primary CTA: `bg-amber-500 hover:bg-amber-600 text-white`
- Secondary: `bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-700`
- Rounded: `rounded-full` or `rounded-xl`
- Touch-friendly padding

## Final Rule

Do not make the UI more decorative.

Make it:

- clearer
- simpler
- more intentional
- more resilient
- more polished
